    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="14">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 14</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="14" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="158" ed="#liebermann"/>Be myneterum. Þridda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_14.lnote.oe.5"/>: þæt an mynet sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_14.lnote.oe.2"/> ofer eall ðæs cynges onweald; ⁊ nan mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_14.lnote.oe.3"/> ne mynetige buton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_14.lnote.oe.3"/> (on<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_14.lnote.oe.6"/>) port.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_14.lnote.oe.4"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="14" corresp="#wit-ld"><pb n="158" ed="#liebermann"/>Be myneterum. We cwædon, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> án mynet sy ofer ealle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_14.lnote.oe.1"/> ðæs cynges anwealde; ⁊ nán man ne mynetige butan port.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="14" corresp="#wit-ot"><pb n="158" ed="#liebermann"/>[Be myneterum.] Þridde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_14.lnote.oe.3-3"/>: þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> an mynet sie ofer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_14.lnote.oe.4-3"/> [ealle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_14.lnote.oe.5-2"/>] þæs cinges<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_14.lnote.oe.6-2"/> anweald; ⁊ nan man ne mynetige butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_14.lnote.oe.7"/> port.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="14" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="159" ed="#liebermann"/>De monetariis.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_14.lnote.oe.2-2"/> Placuit nobis, ut una moneta sit in totum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_14.lnote.oe.3-2"/> regis imperium (regno nostro); et nemo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_14.lnote.oe.4-2"/> (nullus) monetet extra portum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="14" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="134" ed="#attenborough"/>Be myneterum. Ðridda: þæt<ptr type="editorNote" n="16" target="#IIAs_14.attnote.fn.16"/> an mynet sy ofer eall<ptr type="editorNote" n="17" target="#IIAs_14.attnote.fn.17"/> ðæs cynges onweald<ptr type="editorNote" n="18" target="#IIAs_14.attnote.fn.18"/>: ⁊ nan mon ne mynetige buton on port<ptr type="editorNote" n="19" target="#IIAs_14.attnote.fn.19"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="159" ed="#liebermann"/>Von Münzern. Drittens (Wir bestimmten <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi>): dass Eine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_14.lnote.de.1"/> Münze über des Königs ganzes Gebiet hin sei; und niemand münze ausser in einer Stadt.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_14.lnote.de.2"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Of moneyers. Thirdly (We determined, Ld): that there be one coinage throughout all the king's dominion; and that no one mint except in a town.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="135" ed="#attenborough"/>Thirdly: [we declare] that there shall be one coinage throughout the king's realm, and no man shall mint money except in a town<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_14.attnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="421" ed="#whitelock"/>Concerning moneyers. Thirdly, that there is to be one coinage over all the king’s dominion, and no one is to mint money except in a town.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IIIEg_8">III Eg 8</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="316"><ref target="clause:IIIEg_8">III Eg 8–8.2</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_14.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">158</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_14.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">158</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">a <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_14.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">158</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_14.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">158</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_14.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">158</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">am Rande</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in the margin</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_14.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">158</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd.</hi> porte</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to porte</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_14.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">159</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et quot [et <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Br</hi>] in quibus urbibus esse debeant <hi rend="italic">fügt zu MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et quot [et added by Br] in quibus urbibus esse debeant added by MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_14.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">159</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">t. regis i. <hi rend="italic">RT;</hi> toto r. (regno n. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi>) -io <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">t. regis i. RT; toto r. (regno n. Lond) -io MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_14.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">159</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ne. <hi rend="italic">Lond;</hi> nu. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ne. Lond; nu. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_14.lnote.oe.3-3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">158</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">We cwædon <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> þr. <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">We cwædon instead of þr. So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_14.lnote.oe.4-3" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">158</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ofel <hi rend="italic">Ot</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ofel Ot</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_14.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">158</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_14.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">158</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyninges <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyninges So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_14.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">158</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">buton <hi rend="italic">doppelt So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">buton twice So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_14.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">104</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Münze 3. 8. — Diese Stelle benutzt III Eg 8</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Münze 3. 8. — This passage is used by III Eg 8</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_14.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">104</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd.</hi> Stadt 15</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid.</hi> Stadt 15</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_14.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">208</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Besides being a military centre the <hi rend="italic">burh</hi> was the natural centre of trafficking. According to Maitland (<hi rend="italic">Domesday Book and Beyond</hi>, p. 195), when in the laws there is a desire to emphasise the fact that the <hi rend="italic">burh</hi> is a centre of trade, it is called a <hi rend="italic">port</hi>, though not every ‘port’ was necessarily a <hi rend="italic">burh</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_14.attnote.fn.16" n="16" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">134</biblScope></bibl><label>þæt</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">we cwædon þæt</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_14.attnote.fn.17" n="17" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">134</biblScope></bibl><label>eall</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ealle</hi>. Ld, So.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_14.attnote.fn.18" n="18" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">134</biblScope></bibl><label>onweald</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">anwealde</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_14.attnote.fn.19" n="19" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">134</biblScope></bibl><label>port</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">butan port</hi>. Ld, Ot.</seg></note>
      </div>
